# OTTO Platform Rules

## Purpose
- OTTO sits **on top** of each site's ISMS tool (**Intervalid**). It does **not** replace it.
- OTTO syncs site ISMS data into one Group model and provides a consolidated global view.
- Core domain: `Site`, `Document`, `Control`, `SoAEntry`, `Risk`, `Treatment`, `GroupRisk`, `RoadmapItem`, `MaturityScore`, `SyncRecord`.
- Every synced record carries **provenance**: site, source system, last-synced timestamp.

## Stack (do not deviate without being asked)
- **Monorepo**: pnpm workspaces.
- **Web**: React, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind, TanStack Query, React Router, Recharts.
- **API**: NestJS, TypeScript, REST, Prisma, PostgreSQL, class-validator/zod DTOs.
- **Auth**: JWT + RBAC. Roles: `GROUP_ADMIN`, `SITE_OFFICER`, `CONTRIBUTOR`, `AUDITOR`. SSO (OIDC) later.
- **Storage**: S3-compatible (MinIO locally; abstract provider).
- **Containers**: Dockerfile per app; root docker-compose for web, api, postgres, storage.

## Structure
- `apps/web`, `apps/api`, `packages/shared`.
- API: one NestJS module per domain — `isms`, `governance`, `path`, `entities`, `executive`, `sync`, `analytics`, `auth` (controller + service + Prisma repo + DTOs).
- Web: `src/modules/*` mirroring API modules.

## Design system
- Dark executive theme. Colors: midnight `#141B4D` / `#1E2761`, gold `#C9A34E`, ice `#CADCFC`, light `#F3F1EA`, ink `#1B1B1B`.
- Fonts: Playfair Display (headings), Inter (body) via Google Fonts.
- Crown brand motif. Tagline on login + footer: **Inspired by unity. Driven by security.**
- UI must clearly indicate **one site** vs **whole Group** view.

## Coding standards
- Strict TypeScript; avoid `any`. Shared types in `packages/shared`.
- Every API endpoint: RBAC + site-scoping (`SITE_OFFICER` = own site + Group read; `GROUP_ADMIN` = all).
- Small, focused diffs. Comments only where intent is non-obvious.
- New files go in the correct workspace folder per STRUCTURE above.

## Migration note
Legacy scaffold may use `frontend/` and `backend/` — new work should move toward `apps/*` and `packages/shared` when restructuring.
